# Build context hygiene (project-audit item 2).
#
# The Dockerfile copies `backend/` wholesale, so without this file a developer's
# `backend/.env` - which points at the production Supabase database - would be
# baked into the deployed image. Nothing here is needed at run time except the
# application code, `backend/deployment.env` and `backend/requirements.txt`; the
# negations below keep those.

# Environment files and secrets.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!backend/deployment.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
.npmrc
.pypirc

# Local databases and generated artefacts.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
var/
storage/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.log

# VCS, caches, tooling and documentation.
.git
.gitignore
.github
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.idea/
.vscode/
docs/
README.md
render.yaml
vercel.json
Dockerfile
.dockerignore